*	@openeverest/maintainers

# BEGIN contract-adjacent
# Paths where a change can alter what core and its extensions rely on. While
# the contract is unchanged since the last release, a pull request touching
# any of them needs the label contract-change or no-contract-change: see
# contract/MAINTAINING.md. .github/workflows/contract-decision.yaml reads this
# block; list one path per line, anchored at the root.
#
# The contract, and the artifacts its fingerprint covers.
/contract/                                 @openeverest/maintainers
/hack/gen-contract/                        @openeverest/maintainers
/api/                                      @openeverest/maintainers
/config/crd/                               @openeverest/maintainers
# The SDK extensions link, and the schema generator they run.
/provider-runtime/                         @openeverest/maintainers
/pkg/classgen/                             @openeverest/maintainers
# Middleware every API request goes through: it decides, for example,
# which writes reach the webhooks of extensions as a dry run.
/internal/server/middlewares.go            @openeverest/maintainers
# Admission: core's webhooks and admission policies, the API's validation
# handler, and the packages both decide through, which read the class
# validations and Secret definitions extensions declare.
/internal/webhook/                         @openeverest/maintainers
/config/webhook/                           @openeverest/maintainers
/config/policy/                            @openeverest/maintainers
/internal/server/handlers/validation/      @openeverest/maintainers
/internal/backupadmission/                 @openeverest/maintainers
/internal/classvalidation/                 @openeverest/maintainers
/internal/secretdefinition/                @openeverest/maintainers
# Readers of the status extensions write. backup: the Accepted condition
# providers set on BackupClasses, and the status of provider-managed
# Backups, Restores and BackupImports. monitoring: the Accepted condition
# monitoring extensions set on MonitoringClasses, and their conditions on
# MonitoringBindings and MonitoringDestinations. instance, lifecycleevents
# and instancestatus: the Instance status the provider runtime writes.
/internal/controller/backup/               @openeverest/maintainers
/internal/controller/monitoring/           @openeverest/maintainers
/internal/controller/instance/             @openeverest/maintainers
/internal/controller/lifecycleevents/      @openeverest/maintainers
/pkg/instancestatus/                       @openeverest/maintainers
# The connection details Secret the provider runtime writes.
/internal/server/handlers/k8s/instance.go  @openeverest/maintainers
# The in-use finalizers core holds on the objects extensions install.
/internal/controller/inuse/                @openeverest/maintainers
/pkg/inuse/                                @openeverest/maintainers
# END contract-adjacent
